    "created_at": "2024-06-03T13:45:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-06-03T13:45:45Z",
    "body": "Thanks, overall that makes sense as a model to standardize I think. Might need some more thought on how to handle naturally expiring cookies. But perhaps only expiring at the time of a next request or explicit `document.cookie` or Cookie Store API call (I'm assuming those are also synchronization points) is reasonable.\r\n\r\nAs for changes, so if you make multiple changes to a single cookie in a response, you'd only get a single event for only the last change. That's fair, but I don't think that's currently defined at all.",
